      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the label maximum is 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above typical doses of 500\u20131,000 mg. Overdosing raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day), the standard maximum.\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily** (2,000 mg/day).\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intended, please confirm that explicitly. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first. I'll enter the order as soon as I hear back."
      }
     ],
